Package: ESQivive
Title: IVIVE of ADME Parameters for PBK Models
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Susana", "Proença", , "susana.proenca@esqlabs.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Felix", "Mil", , "felix.mil@esqlabs.com", role = "ctb"),
    person("ESQlabs GmbH", role = c("cph", "fnd"))
  )
Description: In vitro to in vivo extrapolation (IVIVE) of absorption,
    distribution, metabolism and excretion (ADME) parameters, to derive
    inputs for physiologically based kinetic (PBK) models. Predicts the
    fraction unbound in microsomal and hepatocyte incubations and in plasma,
    looks up measured fraction unbound values, fits substrate depletion and
    Michaelis-Menten curves, scales in vitro clearance to in vivo, and
    derives intestinal permeability from Caco-2 and effective permeability
    values. The functions are developed for use with the Open Systems
    Pharmacology Suite ('PK-Sim' and 'MoBi').
